-01-08T22:24:26Z","closed_at":"2025-05-09T16:34:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106167","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106167.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106167.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-09T16:34:40Z"},"body":"When we first integrated mbedTLS, we decided not to enable MBEDTLS_THREADING_C (which adds mutex locking to calls modifying the state), and instead to simply create separate contexts (\"states\") for each connection.\r\n\r\nThis worked fine until recently.\r\nSadly, mbedTLS 3 added a global state for the new PSA crypto functionalities (which are required to support TLSv1.3), and this change was originally [not properly reported in the docs](https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/issues/10103#issuecomment-2771869231).\r\nThis results in TLSv1.3 connections accessing and modifying the global state concurrently when running in threads.\r\n\r\nThis commit enables MBEDTLS_THREADING_C, and MBEDTLS_THREADING_C_ALT to provide a generic Godot implementation using the engine Mutex class.\r\n\r\nFixes #104820","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"h